a models phoenix rising the ubisoft game  formerly known as gods and monsters  has a sprawling bright world for you to  explore  fight within and solve puzzles around  despite its surface differences  there's more than a few aspects of the  game that you may find awfully similar  to the legend of zelda breath of the  wild  here are eight of them a bright open  game world  the first thing you'll notice in  immortals is its bright and colorful  world  set in ancient greece immortals has a  giant map to explore  not unlike the kingdom of hyrule there  are massive mountains and dark caves  rolling hills with enemies to take on  and even horses to tame  in our three-hour session with immortals  we only saw one chunk of the map  but we're told there's plenty of diverse  locations to be discovered  from mountainous peaks down to the  cavernous depths of the underworld  game director scott phillips said the  game has been designed with intriguing  landmarks in mind  that'll catch your eye from a distance  and offer up some kind of interesting  experience when you arrive  player driven freedom of exploration  much like breath of the wild your main  objective in immortals phoenix rising is  clear from the outset but where you go  from there is pretty much  up to you your ultimate goal is to save  four gods of ancient greece who've been  defeated at the hands of the big bad  typhon  they're spread out across different  locations around the map but how and  when you choose to proceed is largely up  to the player  and exploration is encouraged voices in  your head  where breath of the wild was punctuated  by the ethereal divine voice of zelda  immortals phoenix rising also pops godly  voices into your head  throughout your journey you'll hear the  voices of zeus and prometheus narrating  your more significant moments  providing commentary and contextualizing  your actions within the larger hero  journey  so this whole story you're telling me  about how you think this mortal named  phoenix has a chance to free all the  gods from typhon's grip  and then destroy him good luck  speaking of which link and phoenix have  a few things in common too  okay so link isn't a demigod with wings  but both protagonists share similar  designs as bright light characters  and each is prophesized to defeat the  evil threatening and corrupting the game  world  stamina and traversal just getting  around the game world will give you  serious breath of the wild vibes  you have a stamina meter that gradually  decreases as you run  or if you're galloping on your horse it  appears you can also climb just about  anything in the game world  but your stamina will drop as you do so  you'll want to be wary of that or risk a  painful landing  luckily and also in the vein of breath  of the wild you can deploy your  brilliant blue demigod wings to glide  down from heights  and there's the option to speed up as  you do there are also potions you can  down halfway up a tricky climb that will  top up your stamina to get you the rest  of the way  that brings us to potion crafting you  can equip  four potions at any one time which do  things like up your stamina and health  the world is filled with resources you  can pick up and munch on for a minor  health increase  but what you'll really want to do is hit  up one of the game's cauldron locations  where you can craft potions using  various combinations of items  just like in breath of the wild puzzles  and shrines  of vaults in addition to being an action  adventure game immortals takes another  page out of breath of the wild's  playbook with its numerous puzzles and  shrines  or vaults as they're known in mortals  players can enter the vaults to take  part in trials of not only strength and  dexterity but also  wits these vaults take place in a  different dimension that is not bound by  the normal rules of the world  which opens up unique possibilities for  puzzles outside of the vaults you can  find puzzle scenarios in the game world  and you can earn special items for  completing them one massive similarity  here  is a mortal's version of breath of the  wild's magnet ability  in immortals you have a number of divine  weapons and abilities  one of which is heracles strength this  allows phoenix to move heavy objects and  magically levitate orbs to solve certain  puzzles in the open world  even the animation where phoenix runs  with hoisted objects above her head  using this ability  is sure to give you serious zelda vibes  unlocking the map  much like towers in breath of the wild  in immortals you'll be on the lookout  for massive statues that you can ascend  to remove the fog from an area of the  map  you'll then need to use the farsight  mechanic to spot locations and mark  icons or simply travel to a point of  interest and then it'll pop up on your  map  game director scott phillips also told  us that there are some soft lock  limitations on traversal  as there are certain skills you might  need to access new areas  or places you can't reach with the  stamina you have fast-paced  flashy combat another major element of  immortals that may give you zelda vibes  is  its combat you're constantly fighting  for survival in the harsh world that's  overrun with monsters of all types  just like in hyrule immortals has a deep  combat system that lets you use multiple  different skills and abilities to lay  waste to your foes  in our playthrough we found that using  your hephaestus hammer ability was  almost always the most effective  approach  for more close quarters combat immortals  offers up light and heavy attacks as  well as a parrying system  players can of course also dodge and  getting the timing just right will slow  down time to help plan your next attack  similar to breath of the wild enemies  are designed as colorful fantastical  monsters  and the greek mythology setting provides  some fun encounters with legendary  creatures as in breath of the wild your  bow is a valuable asset  in one memorable sequence we shot a  cyclops in the eye with an arrow from a  long distance using a special ability  called apollo's arrow  that lets you control the arrow and  guide it in slow motion  let me know what you think of the game  so far in that comment box and stay  tuned for all our coverage on this one  and everything else we saw at the latest  ubisoft forward  you
 

